---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import {
  MessageActionsConversation,
  MessageActionsHandoff,
  MessageActionsPlayground,
  MessageActionsStates,
  MessageActionsTimes,
  MessageActionsVersions,
} from '../../components/MessageActionsDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Message Actions"
  description="Copy, send time, feedback, and regenerate under a chat message, with a switcher for regenerated versions."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Message Actions</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A compact row under a chat message. Copy turns the Markdown into plain text and can add formatted HTML; the send
    time reads as Today, Yesterday, or a date; assistant replies can be rated and regenerated. Message Branch steps
    between regenerated versions.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <MessageActionsPlayground client:only="react" />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Under an assistant reply"
      code={`import { MessageActions } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/message-actions";

<MessageActions
  text={message.text}
  createdAt={message.createdAt}
  feedback={message.feedback}
  onFeedback={(value) => rate(message.id, value)}
  onRetry={() => regenerate(message.id)}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      Only <code>text</code> is required, which shows a single Copy button. Each other prop adds one part:{' '}
      <code>createdAt</code> the time,
      <code>onFeedback</code> the Helpful and Unhelpful toggles, and
      <code>onRetry</code> a Regenerate button. There are no visual variants; icon buttons are ghost{' '}
      <code>icon-sm</code> and Regenerate is a ghost
      <code>sm</code> button. A given rating uses the secondary fill.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>author</code> names the controls: <code>"assistant"</code> (the default) says “response”,{' '}
      <code>"human"</code> says “message”.
      <code>disabled</code> turns off every button, for example while a reply is still running.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">In a conversation</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Hover reveal and formatted copy"
      code={`const entry = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);

<Message align={message.author === "human" ? "end" : "start"}>
  <MessageContent ref={entry}>
    {bubbles}
    <MessageActions
      text={text}
      author={message.author}
      createdAt={message.createdAt}
      hover
      html={() => {
        const parts = entry.current?.querySelectorAll("[data-slot=message-bubble]");
        return parts?.length ? [...parts].map((part) => part.innerHTML).join("") : undefined;
      }}
    />
  </MessageContent>
</Message>`}
    />
    <p>
      With <code>hover</code>, the row stays hidden until the pointer is over the surrounding <code>Message</code> or
      anything in it has focus. On touch screens it is always shown. <code>html</code> runs when Copy is pressed; when
      it returns markup, the clipboard gets both HTML and plain text, so pasting into a document keeps bold, code, and
      links.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <MessageActionsConversation client:only="react" />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Send time</h2>
    <p>
      <code>createdAt</code> is an ISO time shown in the reader’s locale and time zone. Its title gives the full date
      and time.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <MessageActionsTimes client:only="react" />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Versions</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Step between regenerated replies"
      code={`import { MessageActions, MessageBranch } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/message-actions";

<MessageBranch index={index} total={versions.length} onChange={setIndex} />
<MessageActions text={versions[index].text} onRetry={regenerate} />`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>index</code> is zero-based and shown as “2 / 3”. Previous is disabled on the first version and Next on the
      last.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <MessageActionsVersions client:only="react" />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Copy only</h2>
    <p>
      Pass just <code>text</code> under text that is not a chat turn, such as a written handoff in a dialog.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <MessageActionsHandoff client:only="react" />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      After a copy the icon becomes a check and its label says it was copied. If the browser refuses the write, a
      message under the row asks the reader to select the text instead. Choose Blocked to try it; this demo blocks the
      clipboard only while that option is chosen.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <MessageActionsStates client:only="react" />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Actions sit in a group named “Response actions” or “Message actions”; versions in a group named “Response
      versions”. Icon buttons have labels and titles, and the ratings are toggle buttons with
      <code>aria-pressed</code>. A successful copy is announced through a status region and a failed one as an alert.
      The version count is a polite live region. A hover row becomes visible as soon as keyboard focus enters the
      message. It fades in over 120ms, or appears at once when reduced motion is set.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
